Ra&#xFA;l Esparza is on a two-day leave of absence from his starring role in the Broadway musical Galileo after suffering what he says was a &#8220;minor concussion&#8221; during a recent rehearsal.

Michael Park ( Stranger Things, As the World Turns ), the production's alternate Galileo, filled in for Esparza last night and will do so again tonight. Esparza is expected back tomorrow.

In an Instagram video posted yesterday evening, Esparza says, &#8220;Unfortunately, I'm not going to be able to join you for performances of Galileo tonight and tomorrow. The Saturday before we started performances, I suffered a minor concussion in rehearsals, and I still wanted to go on and still wanted to do the show, and it was an amazing week, and I wouldn't have missed it for the world. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News 'The Fantasticks' Review: A Welcome Broadway Debut Seven Decades In The Making News Bryan Cranston & Marianne Jean-Baptiste Heading To Broadway In Ivo Van Hove's Acclaimed 'All My Sons' Revival

