The series chronicles humanity's first contact with an alien civilization. It follows a young woman, whose fateful decision in 1960s China reverberates across space and time into the present day. When the laws of nature inexplicably unravel before their eyes, a close-knit group of brilliant scientists join forces with an unflinching detective to confront the greatest threat in humanity's history. Per the official logline, in Season 2, the alien invasion nears and humanity prepares to meet them &#x2014; on Earth and beyond. While a space fleet embarks on a mission that spans centuries, a secret locked inside of one man's mind might be humanity's only hope for survival.

In addition to Cunningham, Season 2 series regulars include Jess Hong, Benedict Wong, Eiza Gonzalez, Jovan Adepo, Saamer Usmani, Liam Cunningham, Marlo Kelly, Sea Shimooka, Claudia Doumit and Ellie De Lange, with guest stars Alfie Allen, David Yip, Jordan Sunshine and Josh Brener.

Following its 2024 debut, the series spent seven weeks in the Global Top 10, reaching the Top 10 in 93 countries and hitting #1 in 44, with 46.6 million views. Three songs from its soundtrack also reached Billboard's Top TV Songs chart, including Lana Del Rey's "Video Games" at #1.

At the time of the premiere, Benioff, Weiss and Woo confirmed that the drama series would run for three seasons. The number of seasons matches the books in Cixin Liu's trilogy and the trio said that the format will allow them to tell the story as they had intended. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Benioff, Weiss and Woo serve as creators, writers and executive producers on the series. Season 2 executive producers include Bernie Caulfield, Rian Johnson, Ram Bergman, Nena Rodrigue, Qi Lin, Jilong Zhao, Xiaosong Gao, Lauren Ma, Brad Pitt, Jeremy Kleiner, Dede Gardner, Rosamund Pike and Robie Uniacke, Jeremy Podeswa, Miguel Sapochnik and Duncan Muggoch. Jeremy Podeswa and Miguel Sapochnik direct.

Season 2 will premiere on Thursday, January 14 with all six episodes dropping at once.

